Please note, this is a sample solution and the actual code structure of the comment and their corresponding assert method may vary. The output assert statements should not be placed inside this method. It should be in the place where the assert rule should be executed.--------------------You want to collect the assert statements that are present inside the comments that start with "@@@" and they are after PexObserve.ValueForViewing method call. Here is one possible solution that requires regular expression pattern matching and code string splitting to extract the assert statements:

```cs
using System;
using System.IO;
using System.Text.RegularExpressions;

namespace ConsoleApp1
{
    class Program
    {
        static void Main(string[] args)
        {
            string filePath = @"YourFilePath";
            string fileContent = File.ReadAllText(filePath);
            string[] lines = fileContent.Split(new[] {"\r\n", "\n"}, StringSplitOptions.None);

            string pattern = @"PexObserve\.ValueForViewing\(.*?\);.*?(// @@@.*)";
            MatchCollection matches = Regex.Matches(fileContent, pattern);

            foreach (Match match in matches)
            {
                string matchValue = match.Groups[1].ToString();
                Console.WriteLine(matchValue);
            }              
        }
    }
}
```

In the pattern variable, `PexObserve.ValueForViewing\(.*?\);` matches any occurrence of PexObserve.ValueForViewing followed be any characters (`.*?`) until the end of the line. The `(// @@@.*)` at the end matches any occurrence where the comment begins with '@@@' and continues to the end of the line.--------------------Unfortunately, it's not possible to parse the Pex code for comments directly in csharp. Here are the assert statements converted from the Pex code:

